  "body": "## Why\n\nThe **Configure Claude Code** page writes exactly two keys today — `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` and `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`. To grow it into a real guided editor (dropdowns with the actual option lists, a description per setting, permission rules) we first need to know what the full surface is. Nothing in this repo described it, and the upstream surface is large and moves weekly.\n\nSo this lands the reference **and the generator that produces it**, rather than a hand-written snapshot that goes stale the week after it merges.\n\n## What's in it\n\nCaptured at Claude Code **v2.1.228**:\n\n| Surface | Count |\n| --- | --- |\n| Environment variables | 322 |\n| `settings.json` keys (incl. `worktree.*`) | 136 |\n| `permissions.*` keys | 8 + full rule syntax |\n| `sandbox.*` keys | 43 |\n| `~/.claude.json` global config | 6 |\n| `attribution.*` | 3 |\n| Hook events | 29 |\n| Canonical tool names | 44 |\n\nEvery row carries a **Control** column naming the widget the value wants — `toggle`, `select` (with the documented option list), `number`, `path`, `list`, `JSON`, `secret`. That column is the point: it's what lets the page render a real dropdown instead of a text box.\n\n## The traps it documents\n\nA naive editor would do the *opposite* of what the user asked on three classes of value:\n\n- **Six \"set or unset\" variables** — `DISABLE_TELEMETRY`, `DISABLE_ERROR_REPORTING`, `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC`, `CLAUDE_CODE_TMUX_TRUECOLOR`, `FALLBACK_FOR_ALL_PRIMARY_MODELS`, `IS_DEMO`. They read only *whether the variable exists*. Writing `\"0\"` **enables** them. They must be present/absent switches that delete the key.\n- **`FORCE_HYPERLINK`** is parsed as a **number**, so `false` / `no` / `off` all *enable* hyperlinks. Only `0` disables.\n- **Ten credential variables** must be masked and never echoed back.\n\nPlus the things that change what an editor may safely write: scope precedence including the managed-tier ordering, the restrictive-value exceptions that let a lower scope override a managed one, which keys need a restart (`model`, `outputStyle`), and that removing a variable from an `env` block does *not* unset it in a running session.\n\n## Files\n\n- `docs/CLAUDE-CODE-CONFIG.md` — 969-line human reference\n- `docs/claude-code-config-catalog.json` — the same data machine-readable, for the page to build controls from\n- `scripts/gen_claude_config_reference.py` — reads the published markdown of the official pages and emits both. `--fetch` downloads them; without it it reads the gitignored cache, so regeneration is reproducible and CI never needs the network.\n\nClassification is **explicit** wherever the docs state a closed value set. The boolean/number/string split is inferred from the docs' own consistent phrasing (`Set to `1` to …`, `(default: 600000)`, `in milliseconds`), and every inferred decision records its reason in `classification_evidence` — so a wrong guess is visible rather than silent.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full `--fetch` round trip run end to end against the live docs.\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty` all pass on the generator.\n- Full suite: **3718 passed**, 14 failures that reproduce identically on an untouched worktree (6 PowerShell installer, 8 websearch/web-tools — the known local environment baseline).\n\n## Not done\n\nNo production code changed and no page built yet — this is the *input* to that work. `docs/` and a dev-tooling script aren't production paths, so no version bump.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TWCKNkSxNEfus8GfcqXnQD\n",
