    "message": "docs: complete Claude Code configuration reference, generated from upstream docs\n\nThe Configure Claude Code page currently writes two keys, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\nand ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, into settings.json. To grow it into a real editor --\nguided controls, per-setting explanations, dropdowns with the actual option\nlists -- we first need to know what the full surface is. Nothing in this repo\ndescribed it, and the upstream surface is large and moves weekly.\n\nThis adds that reference, and the generator that produces it, rather than a\nhand-written snapshot that goes stale the week after it lands.\n\nWhat it covers, captured at Claude Code v2.1.228:\n\n- 322 environment variables\n- 136 settings.json keys (including the worktree.* group)\n- 8 permissions.* keys and the full permission rule syntax\n- 43 sandbox.* keys\n- 6 ~/.claude.json global-config keys, which settings.json silently ignores\n- 3 attribution.* keys\n- the 29 hook events and the 44 canonical tool names permission rules match\n\nEvery row carries a Control column naming the widget the value wants: toggle,\nselect (with the documented option list), number, path, list, JSON, or secret.\nThat column is the point -- it is what lets the page render a dropdown with\nreal options instead of a text box.\n\nThree classes of value would make a naive editor do the opposite of what the\nuser asked, so they are called out explicitly:\n\n- Six variables (DISABLE_TELEMETRY, DISABLE_ERROR_REPORTING,\n  CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC, CLAUDE_CODE_TMUX_TRUECOLOR,\n  FALLBACK_FOR_ALL_PRIMARY_MODELS, IS_DEMO) read only whether they are set at\n  all. Writing \"0\" enables them. They must be rendered as present/absent\n  switches that delete the key.\n- FORCE_HYPERLINK is parsed as a number, so \"false\" enables hyperlinks.\n- Ten variables carry credentials and must be masked, never echoed back.\n\nAlso documented because they change what an editor may safely write: scope\nprecedence including the managed-tier ordering, the restrictive-value\nexceptions that let a lower scope win, which keys need a restart (model,\noutputStyle), and that removing a variable from an env block does not unset it\nin a running session.\n\nscripts/gen_claude_config_reference.py reads the published markdown of the\nofficial pages and emits both artifacts. --fetch downloads them; without it the\nscript reads the gitignored cache, so regeneration is reproducible and CI never\nneeds the network. Classification is explicit wherever the docs state a closed\nvalue set; the boolean/number/string split is inferred from the docs' own\nconsistent phrasing, and every inferred decision records its reason in\nclassification_evidence so a wrong guess is visible rather than silent.\n\nVerification: full --fetch round trip run end to end against the live docs;\nruff format --check, ruff check and ty all pass on the generator; full suite\n3718 passed with 14 failures that reproduce identically on an untouched\nworktree (6 PowerShell installer, 8 websearch/web-tools -- the known local\nenvironment baseline).\n\nNot done: no production code changed and no page built yet. This is the input\nto that work, not the work. docs/ and a dev-tooling script are not production\npaths, so no version bump.",
